{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1178059-beast-the-primordial-hacks","id":1178059,"title":"Beast the Primordial Hacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-22T06:31:46-08:00","id":1178059,"title":"Beast the Primordial Hacks","content":"Hey I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve seen such a topic except of course Cinder\u2019s excellent analysis.<br /> <br /> Personally some of the hacks/clarifications I do to Beast are<br /> <br /> All Beasts can feed on dreams. Doing so require only to enter your Lair becomes the Horror and hunt through the Primordial Dream. This method has the advantage of providing high-Satiety meals without physical trauma (but has definite mental effects as being fed on by a Beast in your sleep keeps you from regaining Willpower which means repeated feedings drive people mad) and being subtler. Yet by the laws of sympathy the dreams of the persons you know, and presumably love are closer to your Lair than unrelated people.<br /> <br /> A big part of the Beast experience is the exploration of the Primordial Dream and the Astral. Beasts in the Astral have their Horror Form and are the origins of nightmares or dread archetypes.<br /> <br /> More a rule than a hack but I demand the Horrors to be monsters who appear in legends or in recognizable stories. You can have the Slenderman as a Horror but not a bladed shadow by instance. Beast is about in part about myths and legends and your inner monster should reflect that.<br /> <br /> On the same page Hunger must be narrowed down and best be made in accordance to mythic tropes. You don\u2019t hoard everything under the sun, you hoard forbidden knowledge. You don\u2019t punish jaywalkers, you punish kinslayers and find other sinners\u2019 fear a poor meal.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the biggest. Heroes are Beasts whose Horrors are in the image of classical heroes. Now you would think that makes them good guys but heroes have marked the collective unconscious for others reasons than morality. To have Hercules as an Horror (not that Heroes refer to them as such) seems fine and dandy until you remember you\u2019re listening to the desires of someone who killed his wife and children in a fit of madness. This is the reason why most Heroes appears egoists, the Horror in them drive them to be recognized, to gain riches and mates as their due to cleanse the world of monsters. They are more sensitive to Beasts but can hunt anything and even humans they judge corrupt.<br /> <br /> Heroic Hungers are To Rule, To Hunt, To Punish. I don\u2019t see many exemples of Heroes in myths who Hoard or Ruin.<br /> <br /> Heroes have Dreams rather than Nightmares, delusions who generally give their recipients blessings and bonuses. Their Atavisms conjure weapons and equipment but rarely transform them.<br /> <br /> So thoughts? Other hacks you wish to add?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:03:02-08:00","id":1178074,"title":"","content":"There was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1102793-beast-the-alternate-take\">this thread</a>.<br /> <br /> For me, I cast Beasts and Horrors as Legendary Monsters. Namely, I switch their Power Stat to Legend (which is also an Anchor, yes, but something they advance), with Lair an extension of that (a Beast can have a powerful Legend, but not develop their Lair much). The pull of Legend means that mighty Beasts need to be <i>known</i>, which draws Heroes and trouble on its own. Life forms a kind of Integrity meter (again, as well as an Anchor), where it measures how much of a human you are vs being a Monster (bottoming out on it gets you the &quot;Bad&quot; Inheritances). Satiety is pretty much just a Fuel Stat, with Conditions. Anathema are always on and tied to the Horror, as opposed to being something imposed by Heroes. Heroes can easily figure out what they are, and apply extras at higher Legend, though. Family Ties are more about incorporating other monsters into your Legend (or you in theirs, at lower rungs), than about actual familial connections. Beasts are also less &quot;social&quot; and Broods are rarer, dreaded things.<br /> <br /> Basically, I downplay the &quot;Family&quot; angle, and play up the &quot;Monster&quot; angle. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1178059-beast-the-primordial-hacks#post1178059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroic Hungers are To Rule, To Hunt, To Punish. I don\u2019t see many exemples of Heroes in myths who Hoard or Ruin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure there have been Heroes that sought Phat L00t. Jack and the Beanstalk, to borrow from fairy tales, for example. And what are those Rebel heroes that seek to tear down a &quot;corrupt&quot; regime other than those who hunger for Ruin (albeit justified to a subjective degree)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-22-2018, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T14:37:32-08:00","id":1178205,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure I saw something about \u201cDark Lords,\u201d a \u2018lesser\u2019 template mirroring Beasts, who are humans so fearsome and dreaded that they formed a pseudo-Lair around them. Inspired by the baddies from Persona 5, I think. I don\u2019t know who was it, but I found that idea fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T16:52:10-08:00","id":1178270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1178059-beast-the-primordial-hacks?p=1178205#post1178205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure I saw something about \u201cDark Lords,\u201d a \u2018lesser\u2019 template mirroring Beasts, who are humans so fearsome and dreaded that they formed a pseudo-Lair around them. Inspired by the baddies from Persona 5, I think. I don\u2019t know who was it, but I found that idea fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream\">Primordial Dreamscapes</a> thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-22-2018, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}